WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.240
This is the Singularity Daily, for Monday, October 26.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.450
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in AI.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.970
Today felt like growing pains.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.760
Bill Gates calls AI an evolutionary event, like monkeys becoming humans.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.090
He even says his coding skills,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.680
his obsession since age 13, are essentially obsolete.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.370
This week, the owners of Elvis's music sued Anthropic over 274 songs.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.560
From Monday, Sweden's government is blocking ChatGPT and Claude on staff computers,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.180
pointing them to Copilot.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.450
And Reddit's open-source forum just banned any project made with AI,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.410
or made for it.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.040
This week,

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.300
China's Moonshot made its new Kimi model worse at hacking, on purpose.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.040
Now, the money.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.650
OpenAI is reportedly luring Anthropic's big customers away with steep discounts.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.530
At one customer, Rippling,

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.990
OpenAI's share of the coding work jumped from 16 to 52%.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.190
But Apollo's chief economist says that outside tech,

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.070
AI has delivered zero financial payoff so far.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.850
Beyond the seven tech giants, he says,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.830
revenue per worker and profit margins are flat.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.600
Meanwhile,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.010
AI labs are asking faith leaders how to teach chatbots right from wrong.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.200
And Google DeepMind's Lila Ibrahim says answers are cheap now.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.300
Good questions are getting harder.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.060
The catch? Western Australia wants money back from Deloitte,

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.820
over AI-invented sources.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.890
Some of its sums were off by $260 million.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.260
In China, 110 humanoid robots danced in sync for a world record.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.750
In Japan, Tokio Marine will start insuring AI-powered robots next month.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.630
And in Sydney, lawyers complained about stomping upstairs.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.190
It was a young team's human-sized robot.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.250
Growing pains, sure. But you only get those when you're growing.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.480
Want the whole month? Join Peter Xing live in Sydney on October 30.
